module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicTopology.SimplicialObject.Basic
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Grothendieck
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.Coverage
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.CoverLifting
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Simplicial.Defs

/-!
# The total site of a simplicial family of sites

A simplicial family of sites whose transition functors are cocontinuous and whose covering
families have representable pullbacks has a total site. Its underlying category is the
Grothendieck construction, and its coverings are the covering families lying in a single
simplicial degree.

## Main definitions

* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialCoverings.IsCocontinuous`: cocontinuity of every transition
  functor of a simplicial family of sites.
* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialCoverings.total`: the class of componentwise covering families in
  the Grothendieck construction.
* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialCoverings.totalTopology`: the topology generated by these families.

## Implementation notes

The underlying total category is Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.Grothendieck`. Objects and
morphisms therefore have exactly the dependent-pair descriptions in the source. We use the
family-based site axioms `IsSite`, which do not impose the stronger assumption that every pair
of arrows in the total category has a pullback. The associated `GrothendieckTopology` is
generated from those families by `CategoryTheory.topologyOfCoverings`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09WD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09WD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09W7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09W7)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u v a b w

namespace CategoryTheory

namespace SimplicialCoverings

/-- The covering families of the total category: they are precisely componentwise covering
families, embedded using the inclusion of a fibre in the Grothendieck construction. -/
def total (F : SimplicialObject Cat.{v, u})
    (Cov : ∀ n, Covering.{u, v, max u v} (F.obj n) → Prop) :
    Covering.{u, v, max u v} (Grothendieck F) → Prop := fun 𝒰 ↦
  ∃ E : PreZeroHypercover.{max u v} 𝒰.1.fiber,
    Cov 𝒰.1.base ⟨𝒰.1.fiber, E⟩ ∧
      𝒰.2 = E.map (Grothendieck.ι F 𝒰.1.base)

/-- The Grothendieck topology on the total category generated by its componentwise covering
families. -/
def totalTopology (F : SimplicialObject Cat.{v, u})
    (Cov : ∀ n, Covering.{u, v, max u v} (F.obj n) → Prop) :
    GrothendieckTopology (Grothendieck F) :=
  topologyOfCoverings (total F Cov)

/-- The transition functors of a simplicial family of sites are cocontinuous. -/
def IsCocontinuous (F : SimplicialObject Cat.{v, u})
    (Cov : ∀ n, Covering.{u, v, max u v} (F.obj n) → Prop) : Prop :=
  ∀ {m n : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ} (f : m ⟶ n),
    (F.map f).toFunctor.IsCocontinuous (topologyOfCoverings (Cov m))
      (topologyOfCoverings (Cov n))

end SimplicialCoverings

end CategoryTheory

end
